2:[["$","section",null,{"className":"wysiwyg-section py-100 md:py-140","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"container ","children":[["$","h1",null,{"className":"h2 mb-56 text-center","children":["$","$L9",null,{"animateOnScroll":"lines","children":"Privacy Policy · DPDP Act 2023 & RPwD Data Charter"}]}],["$","$La",null,{"className":"max-w-[90rem] mx-auto","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"reset-last wysiwyg--large wysiwyg","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"<p><strong>Effective Date:</strong> January 2026 &nbsp;|&nbsp; <strong>Festival Dates:</strong> 21–23 January 2027 (Vadodara, Gujarat)<br/><strong>Data Fiduciary:</strong> Purple Fest Vadodara 2027 Secretariat — <strong>Praangan Education Trust (Vadodara, Gujarat)</strong>, <strong>Brotherhood (Delhi)</strong> &amp; <strong>Centre for Disabilities Studies and Action, School of Social Work, Tata Institute of Social Sciences (TISS, Mumbai)</strong>.</p>\n<p>Purple Fest Vadodara 2027 is committed to protecting the privacy, autonomy, and dignity of every delegate, speaker, Paralympic athlete, artist, exhibitor, student, and volunteer in full compliance with India’s <strong>Digital Personal Data Protection (DPDP) Act, 2023</strong> and Section 3 (Equality and Non-Discrimination) of the <strong>Rights of Persons with Disabilities (RPwD) Act, 2016</strong>.</p>\n\n<h2>1. Scope of This Privacy Notice</h2>\n<p>This Privacy Notice applies to all personal and accessibility accommodation data collected through the Purple Fest Vadodara 2027 digital portal (<a href=\"https://www.purplefestivalvadodara.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">www.purplefestivalvadodara.com</a>), the Delegate Pass (₹2,200) registration workflow, the Tier A–D Exhibition Stall booking desk, the GIEN &amp; TISS Academic Abstract portal, and on-ground registration counters at <strong>The Maharaja Sayajirao University, Vadodara</strong> and <strong>GMERS Medical College, Gotri, Vadodara</strong>.</p>\n\n<h2>2. Categories of Personal Data We Collect</h2>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>Identity &amp; Credential Data:</strong> Full name, organization/institution/DPO affiliation, designation, city/state, email address, and mobile number.</li>\n  <li><strong>Registration &amp; Financial Data:</strong> Selected pass category (Mandatory ₹2,200 Delegate Pass) or Exhibition Stall Tier (Tier A ₹15,000 / Tier B ₹35,000 / Tier C ₹12,000 / Tier D ₹5,500), invoice/GST details, and payment transaction reference.</li>\n  <li><strong>Voluntary Accessibility &amp; RPwD Accommodation Data:</strong> Only where voluntarily disclosed by you to arrange on-ground support across any of the <strong>21 Benchmark Disabilities (RPwD Act 2016)</strong>—such as Indian Sign Language (ISL) interpretation, Braille/large-print kits, wheelchair/mobility-scooter charging, tactile guidance, quiet sensory sanctuary access, or medical/hemophilia/thalassemia cold-chain storage.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>3. Strict Purpose Limitation for Disability &amp; Accommodation Data</h2>\n<p>Your voluntary accessibility disclosures are used <strong>exclusively</strong> by the Purple Fest Accessibility &amp; Inclusion Logistics Desk to provision reasonable accommodations during 21–23 January 2027. We <strong>never</strong> sell, rent, monetize, or share individual disability or health-accommodation records with commercial sponsors, advertisers, or unauthorized third parties.</p>\n\n<h2>4. Browser LocalStorage &amp; Accessibility Preferences</h2>\n<p>Our website stores your accessibility preferences (such as reduced-motion settings, high-contrast mode, Deal Sizer / Stall Calculator scenarios, and saved festival itinerary) locally in your browser’s <code>localStorage</code> so your experience remains barrier-free across sessions without tracking you across external websites.</p>\n\n<h2>5. Legal Basis Under the DPDP Act 2023</h2>\n<p>We process your personal data based on your explicit, affirmative consent provided at the time of form submission and for the legitimate fulfillment of your Delegate Pass (₹2,200) or Exhibition Stall registration.</p>\n\n<h2>6. Data Sharing with Coalition Partners</h2>\n<p>Where you submit an academic paper for the <strong>GIEN &amp; TISS Inclusive Education Conclave</strong> or register for a <strong>Para-Sports Championship</strong>, relevant submission details are shared strictly with the respective review committee (Global Inclusive Education Network, Tata Institute of Social Sciences, or the Para-Sports Technical Directorate) for scheduling and certification.</p>\n\n<h2>7. Data Security &amp; Encryption</h2>\n<p>All registration records and accommodation requests are stored in encrypted access-controlled databases restricted to authorized Secretariat personnel who have signed the Purple Fest Confidentiality &amp; Dignity Pledge.</p>\n\n<h2>8. Data Retention &amp; Post-Festival Archiving</h2>\n<p>Specific on-ground accommodation requests (such as dietary, sensory, or medical support notes) are permanently purged within <strong>60 days</strong> after the conclusion of Purple Fest Vadodara 2027 (by 24 March 2027), while participation certificates and statutory accounting records for ₹2,200 Delegate Passes and Tier A–D Stalls are retained as required by Indian tax and audit laws.</p>\n\n<h2>9. Your Rights as a Data Principal</h2>\n<p>Under the DPDP Act 2023, you have the right to access a summary of your personal data, correct or update your badge/accommodation details, withdraw consent, or request erasure by writing to our Data Protection &amp; Accessibility Officer.</p>\n\n<h2>10. Children &amp; Student Delegations</h2>\n<p>Registrations for school students and minors with disabilities participating in Purple Kaleidoscope, Inclusive Youth Parliament, or adaptive sports must be submitted with verifiable parent/guardian or authorized school-head consent.</p>\n\n<h2>11. Accessibility of Privacy Communications</h2>\n<p>Upon request, this Privacy Notice and all consent forms are available in <strong>Accessible PDF (Screen-Reader Tagged), Grade-1 English/Gujarati Braille, Large Print (18pt+), and Indian Sign Language (ISL) video summary</strong>.</p>\n\n<h2>12. Contact the Data Protection &amp; Accessibility Desk</h2>\n<p><strong>Purple Fest Vadodara 2027 Secretariat</strong><br/><strong>Address:</strong> Praangan Education Trust, 1st Floor, Trimurti Apartments, Baroda Imaging Lab Lane, Near Mahalakshmi Store, Alkapuri, Vadodara, Gujarat<br/><strong>Organisers:</strong> Praangan (Vadodara, Gujarat) · Brotherhood (Delhi) · Centre for Disabilities Studies and Action, School of Social Work, Tata Institute of Social Sciences (Mumbai)<br/><strong>Knowledge Partner:</strong> State Commission for Persons with Disabilities, Goa &nbsp;|&nbsp; <strong>Venue Partners:</strong> The Maharaja Sayajirao University, Vadodara &amp; GMERS Medical College, Gotri, Vadodara<br/><strong>Email:</strong> <a href=\"mailto:purplefestivalvadodara@gmail.com\">purplefestivalvadodara@gmail.com</a> &nbsp;|&nbsp; <strong>Website:</strong> <a href=\"https://www.purplefestivalvadodara.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">www.purplefestivalvadodara.com</a><br/><strong>Contact Persons &amp; Helpline:</strong> Radha Tandon (<a href=\"tel:+919974383920\">+91 99743 83920</a>) &nbsp;|&nbsp; Satish Kapoor (<a href=\"tel:+919899472065\">+91 98994 72065</a>, <a href=\"tel:+919211760202\">+91 92117 60202</a>)</p>"}}]}]]}]}]]
